{
  "id": "graceful-degradation",
  "term": "graceful degradation",
  "definition": "In cognition and neural network accounts, graceful degradation refers to a gradual reduction in performance when a system is damaged or when input is noisy or distorted, with some function still preserved rather than failing all at once. It is used to describe patterns of impairment seen in language and other cognitive functions.",
