      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports the idea that PDP accounts for “preservation of function in the face of noisy or distorted input” and mentions “the phenomenon of graceful degradation” in language impairment studies (e.g., from stroke or dementia), but it does not explicitly state that the performance reduction is “gradual” or describe the reduction as gradual.",
        "The definition’s framing “when a system is damaged or when input is noisy or distorted” is only partially supported: the packet mentions impairment from stroke/dementia and preservation with noisy/distorted input, but it does not connect these to the specific “gradual reduction in performance” phrasing."
